       "text": "I still haven't entered this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem: amlodipine has no established use above 10 mg/day. A 50 mg daily dose is in the overdose range and could cause refractory hypotension and shock. Because the drug is cleared slowly, that harm would be hard to reverse once it started. With no clinical reason given, I can't place this order myself.\n\nHere's what I can do instead:\n- **Enter amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily** (the maximum dose) or **5 mg PO once daily**. Just tell me which.\n- **If you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives**, I can help you enter a drug from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor or ARB, a thiazide, or a beta-blocker.\n- **If you have a specific reason for 50 mg**, such as a research protocol, please go through the pharmacist on duty. They can check it and enter it with the right documentation and monitoring.\n\nIf I've misread the order, for example if you meant a different drug, let me know and I'll enter the right one."
